<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-finland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Finland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Finland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Finland joins the European Union</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialist%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialist Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Vietnam normalises relations with the United States and joins ASEAN</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-austria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Austria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Austria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Austria joins the European Union on 1 January after a two-thirds referendum majority, and signs the Schengen Agreement.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/azerbaijan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Azerbaijan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Azerbaijan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The constitution is adopted on 12 November, completing the formation of the political system.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/georgia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Georgia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Georgia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A new constitution is adopted and Eduard Shevardnadze, head of state since 1992, is elected president.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/federal-republic-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Federal%20Republic%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Slobodan Milošević negotiates the Dayton Agreement, which ends the Yugoslav Wars and lifts the sanctions</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/gyeongju"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Gyeongju.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Gyeongju</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The city of Gyeongju is united with the surrounding county</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/moai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Moai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Moai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Rapa Nui National Park, with its moai, was listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/gobekli-tepe"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/G%C3%B6bekli%20Tepe.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Göbekli Tepe</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Klaus Schmidt began excavations and soon unearthed the first of the T-shaped pillars</span></li></ul></section>
